{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/653956-beasts-with-multiple-hungers","id":653956,"title":"Beasts with multiple Hungers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-06T08:50:01-07:00","id":653956,"title":"Beasts with multiple Hungers","content":"The way I understand it, Hunger works rather like the Y-splat for Beasts. Now, to my knowledge several kinds of other supernaturals (vampires, mages, and changelings come to mind) can effectively mix and match one of their splats with the appropriate Merit (vampires and mages can belong to multiple Covenants or Orders by buying the appropriate Status merit, changelings can have multiple kiths by buying the Dual Kith merit or by means of Wyrd evolution). By analogy, I was wondering about a Beast being awakened with or developing multiple Hungers. Thematically it seems to me there would be no obstacle to an Horror developing a less specialized appetite and being able to be sated by different kinds of fear. From a playstyle PoV it would allow the Beast to swap its hunting methods (for convenience or variety's sake) from time to time without having to rely on Family Dinner. Of course the ability to have multiple Hungers would have to paid for with a Merit, but it seems to me there would be most Hunger pairings could combine well in the same character (e.g. Prey and Ruin if the Horror focuses on being a destroyer, Collection and Prey if it focuses on being a hunter, Power and Punishment if it gets its kicks from being dominator, judge, and executioner). By analogy with Dual Kith and Hunger Management I'd price such a Merit three dots. I'm creatively challenged about the name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 09-06-2015, 12:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T09:43:20-07:00","id":654025,"title":"","content":"I was actually thinking about this too... only I'd make it an Incarnate Ability, since it basically doubles your options for how to regain Satiety. Seems too powerful to be a Merit, to me. If you do make it a Merit, then feeding should probably be more difficult.<br /> <br /> For a name, how about &quot;Acquired Taste?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T09:59:07-07:00","id":654041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/653956-beasts-with-multiple-hungers#post653956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, to my knowledge several kinds of other supernaturals (vampires, mages, and changelings come to mind) can effectively mix and match one of their splats with the appropriate Merit (vampires and mages can belong to multiple Covenants or Orders by buying the appropriate Status merit, changelings can have multiple kiths by buying the Dual Kith merit or by means of Wyrd evolution).</div> </div> </div> </div>Changeling kiths are not a Y-splat. They are either a subdivision of the X-splat (in 1e) or the X-splat itself (in 2e).<br /> <br /> Your other two points of comparison fail on the grounds that they're political organizations with proprietary magic. Hungers are closer to mummy Guilds in terms of metaphysical centrality and changeability.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> By analogy with Dual Kith and Hunger Management I'd price such a Merit three dots. </div> </div> </div>Tack a Lair prerequisite on it and/or make it a scaling Merit with the drawback of moving the boundary between Sated and Gorged up the scale.<br /> <br /> For instance:<br /> <br /> <b>Broad Palate (\u2022 or \u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisite:</b> Lair 3 (\u2022) or 6 (\u2022\u2022)<br /> <b>Effect:</b> This Merit gives your character an additional Hunger they can gain Satiety from. At one dot, this extra Hunger can only be satisfied when the Beast is Ravenous or Starving, while at two dots the extra Hunger provides sustenance when the character is Sated as well.<br /> <b>Drawback:</b> The character's Broad Palate dots are added to their threshold for Low Satiety for the purposes of Inflicting Nightmares (i.e. at two dots the character's Horror goes wandering for sustenance at Satiety 5 or lower). Additionally, the character adds their Broad Palate dots to the threshold for High Satiety for the purposes of gaining and resolving Satiety Conditions (i.e. at one dot the character must reach Satiety 8 to resolve the Sated Condition and gain the Gorged Condition).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T11:08:08-07:00","id":654095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/653956-beasts-with-multiple-hungers?p=654041#post654041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tack a Lair prerequisite on it and/or make it a scaling Merit with the drawback of moving the boundary between Sated and Gorged up the scale.<br /> <br /> For instance:<br /> <br /> <b>Broad Palate (\u2022 or \u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisite:</b> Lair 3 (\u2022) or 6 (\u2022\u2022)<br /> <b>Effect:</b> This Merit gives your character an additional Hunger they can gain Satiety from. At one dot, this extra Hunger can only be satisfied when the Beast is Ravenous or Starving, while at two dots the extra Hunger provides sustenance when the character is Sated as well.<br /> <b>Drawback:</b> The character's Broad Palate dots are added to their threshold for Low Satiety for the purposes of Inflicting Nightmares (i.e. at two dots the character's Horror goes wandering for sustenance at Satiety 5 or lower). Additionally, the character adds their Broad Palate dots to the threshold for High Satiety for the purposes of gaining and resolving Satiety Conditions (i.e. at one dot the character must reach Satiety 8 to resolve the Sated Condition and gain the Gorged Condition).</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems an excellent writeup for the idea. The Lair prerequisite and the drawbacks make sense. I am just concerned that to combine a Lair prerequisite and a double drawback at both ends of the Satiety scale may be a bit too much for the benefits the Merit provides. After all, it does nothing more for the Beast than allowing an extra means of Satiety supply that does not carry the social baggage of Family Dinner. And the latter comes free. I would either drop the Lair prerequisite or one of the drawbacks, most likely the Low Satiety one. It seems a little less appropriate than the High Satiety one. As things stand, however, your writeup is not so unbalanced as to be unplayable.<br /> <br /> Optimally, I would make this Merit available to normal Beasts and a different version with no drawbacks as an Incarnate ability.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T11:15:05-07:00","id":654100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WarDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/653956-beasts-with-multiple-hungers?p=654025#post654025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was actually thinking about this too... only I'd make it an Incarnate Ability, since it basically doubles your options for how to regain Satiety. Seems too powerful to be a Merit, to me. If you do make it a Merit, then feeding should probably be more difficult.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, this Merit would allow an extra means of Satiety that is somewhat easier to use than Family Dinner, but not radically more so. Since Family Dinner comes free, and Hunger Management already allows a Beast an important degree of control on its Satiety supply, I see this ability as far from too powerful to be a Merit. I agree it may come with some kind of drawback, and Satchel's writeup provides some good ideas in this regard, although I'm concerned it overcharges the ability. As it concerns Incarnates, I totally agree. I would actually make this ability available in two forms, a Merit with some costs and an Incarnate Ability with no drawbacks. Much the same way several Beast powers do exist both as Atavisms and Incarnate Abilities.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T19:26:40-07:00","id":655832,"title":"","content":"You do make good points there... in fact, here's an idea for an alternate write-up of the Merit. Kinda grasping at straws on the prerequisites. Maybe Wits would be a better fit?<br /> <br /> <b>Acquired Taste (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisite:</b> Beast, Lair 3, Occult 2<br /> <b>Effect:</b> This Merit gives your character a second Hunger, an alternate method of gaining Satiety.<br /> <b>Drawback:</b> The Horror's newly expanded palate makes it finicky; meals that would leave most Beasts replete become unsatisfying. All feeding rolls take a -2 penalty, unless the situation is one that somehow satisfied both Hungers. For example, a Tyrant/Collector would have to establish dominance in the process of acquiring something new in order to fully match his Horror's tastes. Family Dinner is unaffected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T01:16:27-07:00","id":656209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/653956-beasts-with-multiple-hungers?p=654100#post654100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, this Merit would allow an extra means of Satiety that is somewhat easier to use than Family Dinner, but not radically more so.</div> </div> </div> </div> Not necessarily, no. You might theoretically have more opertunities to feed your Hunger, but at Low Satiety, its really easy to feed any of the Hungers, since its just a matter of a turn or so to set it up. Medium and High Satiety simply take too long (full scene or session) for having two different Hungers to feed to matter - still takes effort and planning to find them.<br /> <br /> Family Dinner is still much more effective means of feeding at Medium and High Satiety than using your Hunger, no matter how many of the Hunger groups you might have to - the Horror is just too picky at those levels on what it wants to feed on.<br /> <br /> In some games, like Demon and Geist, your innate splat (Incarnation and Threshold) don't hold a lot of thematic weight, and its easy to run things as if the divisions were all in someone's head. That's also true in Beast, but with the philosophy splat instead of innate - Hunger just doesn't hold a lot of weight. There's little to no mechanics attached to each Hunger, no social organization, no real benefit. Hells, you could easily run the game with everyone having access to every Hunger from the start, and it wouldn't affect the game very much.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T04:50:48-07:00","id":656381,"title":"","content":"Seems kind of strange to say Hunger doesn't hold a lot of thematic weight when it's one of the main themes of Beast. It heavily informs the inhuman need of the player characters and its specific inclination beyond just base fear, and by extension how the Begotten likely deals with it and the brunt of his methods as a terror-sower. Absolutely true that it doesn't have much mechanical weight, but I feel that it's narratively very important. A fair bit more so than Incarnation and Threshold.<br /> <br /> (Unless you only meant that it's easy to run things as though the division was all in someone's head, in which case ignore this post.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 09-08-2015, 07:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T05:06:10-07:00","id":656390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/653956-beasts-with-multiple-hungers?p=656209#post656209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Not necessarily, no. You might theoretically have more opertunities to feed your Hunger, but at Low Satiety, its really easy to feed any of the Hungers, since its just a matter of a turn or so to set it up. Medium and High Satiety simply take too long (full scene or session) for having two different Hungers to feed to matter - still takes effort and planning to find them.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's one way it could matter, in that at as Satiety increases, it becomes far harder to feed ethically; at High Satiety, it borders on the impossible. If you want to restrict yourself to not hurting anyone (or not hurting anyone too badly), or feeding on people who deserve (or &quot;deserve&quot;) it in some fashion, an addition Hunger can be a boon.<br /> <br /> How would you modify Broad Palate to cover a Beast who's second Hunger only kicks in a Mid and High? (That is, the second Hunger is a delicacy their Horror likes when it's relatively full, but means little to it when it's Starving or Ravenous)?<br /> <br /> Incidentally, my instinct is against having a Lair level be a prerequisite for Broad Palate or Acquired Taste. Hungers seem a but more innate than your average Y-splat, almost like Beasts have two X's - yes, I know Hunger can change, but it's not a routine thing - as such, I don't really see multiple ones being something you can learn with power.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T17:05:54-07:00","id":657154,"title":"","content":"It should probably have some kind of prerequisite, though (and you can have two Lair dots at chargen). What would you suggest instead?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T06:50:39-07:00","id":657811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WarDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/653956-beasts-with-multiple-hungers?p=657154#post657154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It should probably have some kind of prerequisite, though (and you can have two Lair dots at chargen). What would you suggest instead?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really have a better idea. Maybe Lair 2, but must be taken at character generation (in story terms, it's the other way round: multiple ways to eat and build itself up is why the Horror is stronger than most).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T07:23:16-07:00","id":657852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/653956-beasts-with-multiple-hungers?p=656381#post656381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems kind of strange to say Hunger doesn't hold a lot of thematic weight when it's one of the main themes of Beast. It heavily informs the inhuman need of the player characters and its specific inclination beyond just base fear, and by extension how the Begotten likely deals with it and the brunt of his methods as a terror-sower. Absolutely true that it doesn't have much mechanical weight, but I feel that it's narratively very important. A fair bit more so than Incarnation and Threshold.</div> </div> </div> </div> The divisions are entirely artificial. Feeding your Hunger is thematic. Having to divide it into five different categories and only taking one? Not very. <br /> <br /> I mean, lets pretend we're playing a dragon. Collection, check. Dragons are also known for their rages and destroying the country side. Ruin, check. Being a badass predator? Check. Ambitious and domineering? Tyrannt, check. They all fit a stereotypical dragon character. Why so limited? Because reasons. The division of Hungers doesn't hold a lot of weight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T12:59:31-07:00","id":658292,"title":"","content":"I largely agree Beast is a game where splat divisions just don't hold much thematic weight (one important reason why I fancy it). As MCN pointed out, feeeding your Hunger is quite thematic. But the divisions between Hunger categories feel quite artificial and it's easy to blur lines between them. The game could have just as easily (and artificially) tried to create splats by using Lessons instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T14:07:24-07:00","id":658370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/653956-beasts-with-multiple-hungers?p=656390#post656390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's one way it could matter, in that at as Satiety increases, it becomes far harder to feed ethically; at High Satiety, it borders on the impossible. If you want to restrict yourself to not hurting anyone (or not hurting anyone too badly), or feeding on people who deserve (or &quot;deserve&quot;) it in some fashion, an addition Hunger can be a boon.<br /> <br /> How would you modify Broad Palate to cover a Beast who's second Hunger only kicks in a Mid and High? (That is, the second Hunger is a delicacy their Horror likes when it's relatively full, but means little to it when it's Starving or Ravenous)?</div> </div> </div> </div>You have a point about the main usefulness of Broad Palate - i.e. it essentially gets useful in order to have a second option at Mid or High Satiety. Since the point of having a second Hunger seems related with the notion of a broad palate and rather at odds with the one of having a finicky palate in a thematic and gameplay sense, and the Hunger divisions are kinda artificial to begin with, I think the Broad Palate version realizes the concept better than the Acquired Taste one (even if it may use some adjustments). For the same reasons this ability should be available all the way from Low to High Satiety, even if it gets more useful towards the latter end of the spectrum. I also strongly disagree with limiting it to character creation only, since I see no real thematic reason why the Beast couldn't learn to adjust its Horror's tastes, the divisions between Hungers don't have much importance to begin with, and by compelling analogy with Hunger Management which has no such restriction.<br /> <br /> I would propose this writeup:<br /> <br /> <b>Broad Palate (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisite:</b> Beast, Composure 3, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Effect:</b> This Merit gives your character a second Hunger, an alternate method of gaining Satiety.<br /> <b>Drawback:</b> The Horror's expanded palate makes it gluttonous. Add +1 to the character's threshold for Low Satiety for the purposs of Inflicting Nightmares (i.e. the character's Horror goes wandering for sustenance at Satiety 4 or lower). Additionally, the character adds +1 to the threshold for High Satiety for the purposes of gaining and resolving Satiety Conditions (i.e. the character must reach Satiety 8 to resolve the Sated Condition and gain the Gorged Condition).<br /> <br /> It seems to me the psychic resilience traits may be the best ones to work as prerequisites for this Merit (also by analogy with Hunger Management), and if we combine two of them (and price the Merit at 3) we can safely avoid a Lair one, and tone down the Drawback's severity in comparison to Satchel's version (although his general idea still seems the best one so far for a Drawback).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 09-10-2015, 08:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T14:17:43-07:00","id":658374,"title":"","content":"I still find the Hunger divisions quite important, but it's very much true that there's overlap. Then again I'm biased, because I enjoy the concept that different sorts of fear have different tastes. Do agree that one victim's fear might satisfy more than one Beast, each with different preferences, and another's might not satisfy two Begotten that do have the same preference. It makes sense you could dredge distinct impressions of fear from the same reaction, especially if it depends on how the Beast involved classifies their favored meal. So yeah, logical overlap but important distinction between characters, in my opinion.<br /> <br /> Had the impression the lessons bit came later in the design process of Beast, though. Or maybe not, based on what some of the writers said. I wouldn't have been opposed to the nature of the Primordial Dream as a source of wisdom through grim lessons and monstrous channels (as well as the relation of Heroes to it as of the last rewrite) coming with a perception-defying supplement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 09-09-2015, 05:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T14:47:36-07:00","id":658398,"title":"","content":"*shrugs* Sure, each Hunger is personalized to each beast. Which, imho, makes the divisions even more arbitrary - there's zero reason for two Collectors to be remotely the same. Frankly, I think that your Legend would serve as a better guideline for the ways you feed your Satiety than your Hunger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T16:22:58-07:00","id":658597,"title":"","content":"I make a clear division in my head between <i>how</i>* you sate your Hunger and <i>what</i> your palate demands from the meal, but fair enough.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">*Though I must incidentally admit I was hoping the Legend trait would have more prominent impact on the way a Beast is and develops.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}